{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 31,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I made a covenant with mine eyes;\nHow then should I look upon a virgin?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For what is the portion from God above,\nAnd the heritage from the Almighty on high?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is it not calamity to the unrighteous,\nAnd disaster to the workers of iniquity?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Doth not he see my ways,\nAnd number all my steps?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have walked with falsehood,\nAnd my foot hath hasted to deceit",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(Let me be weighed in an even balance,\nThat God may know mine integrity);",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If my step hath turned out of the way,\nAnd my heart walked after mine eyes,\nAnd if any spot hath cleaved to my hands:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then let me sow, and let another eat;\nYea, let the produce of my field be rooted out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If my heart hath been enticed unto a woman,\nAnd I have laid wait at my neighbor’s door;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then let my wife grind unto another,\nAnd let others bow down upon her.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For that were a heinous crime;\nYea, it were an iniquity to be punished by the judges:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it is a fire that consumeth unto Destruction,\nAnd would root out all mine increase.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have despised the cause of my man-servant or of my maid-servant,\nWhen they contended with me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What then shall I do when God riseth up?\nAnd when he visiteth, what shall I answer him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Did not he that made me in the womb make him?\nAnd did not one fashion us in the womb?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have withheld the poor from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " desire,\nOr have caused the eyes of the widow to fail,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or have eaten my morsel alone,\nAnd the fatherless hath not eaten thereof",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(Nay, from my youth he grew up with me as with a father,\nAnd her have I guided from my mother’s womb);",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have seen any perish for want of clothing,\nOr that the needy had no covering;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If his loins have not blessed me,\nAnd if he hath not been warmed with the fleece of my sheep;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless,\nBecause I saw my help in the gate:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then let my shoulder fall from the shoulder-blade,\nAnd mine arm be broken from the bone.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For calamity from God is a terror to me,\nAnd by reason of his majesty I can do nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have made gold my hope,\nAnd have said to the fine gold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Thou art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my confidence;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have rejoiced because my wealth was great,\nAnd because my hand had gotten much;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have beheld the sun when it shined,\nOr the moon walking in brightness,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And my heart hath been secretly enticed,\nAnd my mouth hath kissed my hand:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This also were an iniquity to be punished by the judges;\nFor I should have denied the God that is above.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have rejoiced at the destruction of him that hated me,\nOr lifted up myself when evil found him",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(Yea, I have not suffered my mouth to sin\nBy asking his life with a curse);",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If the men of my tent have not said,\nWho can find one that hath not been filled with his meat?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(The sojourner hath not lodged in the street;\nBut I have opened my doors to the traveller);",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If like Adam I have covered my transgressions,\nBy hiding mine iniquity in my bosom,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because I feared the great multitude,\nAnd the contempt of families terrified me,\nSo that I kept silence, and went not out of the door—",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that I had one to hear me!\n(Lo, here is my signature, let the Almighty answer me)\nAnd ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that I had",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the indictment which mine adversary hath written!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely I would carry it upon my shoulder;\nI would bind it unto me as a crown:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I would declare unto him the number of my steps;\nAs a prince would I go near unto him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If my land crieth out against me,\nAnd the furrows thereof weep together;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have eaten the fruits thereof without money,\nOr have caused the owners thereof to lose their life:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.31.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let thistles grow instead of wheat,\nAnd cockle instead of barley.The words of Job are ended.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
